From: momokind <momokind2002@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] [VideoPlayer] Render 10-bit HDR10/SDR output and cap its static metadata

The tone-mapping output modes now scan out 10-bit RGB (XRGB2101010) where
the mode's link has room and the video plane advertises the format: the
RK3588 HDMI glue runs TMDS only (no FRL), so 10-bit RGB's 1.25x pixel
clock only fits up to 4K30 (and 1080p120), and its VOP2 Esmart planes take
no 10-bit RGB while the Cluster planes take it only AFBC-compressed, so
linear XRGB2101010 falls back to 8-bit there. The renderer picks the
depth from the current mode, recreates the tunnel when it changes, and
stages the connector's max bpc accordingly (the DV tunnel keeps its own
8-bit).

For HDR10 output, cap the static metadata at target_nits when the engine
tone-maps: the source's mastering peak and MaxCLL/MaxFALL would make the
sink tone-map a second time. The per-frame RPU L1 tone mapping is the
engine's; the static metadata should describe what is left of it.

